<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila firms sell oil stake to Texaco unit.</title>
<headline>Manila firms sell oil stake to Texaco unit.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five Manila companies said on Wednesday they were selling their stakes in an oil exploration block in Thailand to Texaco Exploration (Thailand) Ltd, a unit of U.S.-based Texaco Inc.</p>
<p>Basic Petroleum &amp; Minerals Inc said in a statement it was selling its 12.346 percent stake in Thailand's Block 12/32 oil exploration area for $740,760.</p>
<p>Palawan Oil &amp; Gas Exploration Inc and First Abacus Financial Holdings Corp said in a joint statement they were each selling their five percent stakes to Texaco for $300,000 apiece.</p>
</text>
